Governance Architecture Integration Note
1. Overview:
  This document defines governance checkpoints across the AI system to ensure safe, compliant, and controlled execution of actions.

2. Governance Checkpoints Mapping:
a. GenAI Prompt Layer
  *Input validation is applied to user prompts
  *Unsafe or restricted prompts are blocked

b. Agent Orchestration Layer
  *Risk classification is performed
  *Policies (OPA) evaluate actions
  *High-risk actions require approval

c. DevOps / Execution Layer
  *Only approved actions are executed
  *Deployment pipelines enforce governance rules

3. Integration Touchpoints

Pre-Execution Validation
  *Input validation
  *Policy evaluation (OPA)
  *Risk-based decision (allow/block)

Post-Execution Logging

Logs include agent ID, action, decision

Enables audit and traceability

4. Future Compliance Extensions

GDPR (Data Privacy)

Data masking and privacy enforcement

Restrict storage of personal data

HIPAA (Healthcare Compliance)

Secure handling of medical data

Role-based access control

5. Conclusion

The governance framework ensures controlled AI execution through validation, policy enforcement, and logging. It provides clear interaction boundaries and supports future compliance integration.
